{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Tries"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","title":"Tries","externalID":"Tries"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Sets of sequences","anchor":"Sets-of-sequences","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree"]},{"title":"Dictionaries keyed by sequences","anchor":"Dictionaries-keyed-by-sequences","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary"]},{"title":"Pattern matching","anchor":"Pattern-matching","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton"]},{"title":"Extended Modules","anchor":"Extended-Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trees"],"generated":true}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is a set of sequences and a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" a dictionary keyed by them, both kept in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a trie (Fredkin, 1960): a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose root-to-vertex paths spell the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keys. They answer the queries a hash set cannot: every key with a prefix"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"elements(withPrefix:)"},{"type":"text","text":", whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"count"},{"type":"text","text":" is O(1)), whether any key has one ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hasPrefix(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"), and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the longest key that is a prefix of a query ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"longestPrefix(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import Tries","","let words = Trie([\"car\", \"cart\", \"cat\", \"dog\"])","words.contains(\"cat\")                                   \/\/ true","words.elements(withPrefix: \"car\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ [\"car\", \"cart\"]","words.longestPrefix(of: \"carton\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ \"cart\""],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keys are any sequence of the symbol type and are stored as "},{"code":"[Symbol]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". For text, the symbol"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type decides what a step is: "},{"code":"Trie<Character>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" steps by grapheme cluster, "},{"code":"Trie<Unicode.Scalar>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by scalar, and "},{"code":"Trie<UInt8>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" over "},{"code":"utf8","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" by byte, the fastest of the three, because comparing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bytes is cheaper than comparing "},{"code":"Character","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s. When the symbols are "},{"code":"Comparable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", each vertex keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its children sorted, so iteration is in lexicographic order; otherwise children come in the order"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they were added."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" hold the same keys and answer the same queries,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with the same names, in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): every chain of vertices with one child and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its symbols, so there is a vertex per key and per"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"branching point rather than per symbol. They suit keys with long shared prefixes, such as file"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"paths or URLs, and build faster and in less memory than a trie of the same keys."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A trie’s shape converts to Grafluent’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"PrefixTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":"PrefixTree(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and a radix tree’s to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Arborescence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of its vertices’ prefixes with ","type":"text"},{"code":"Arborescence(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (import Grafluent’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Trees","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"module beside this one).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (Aho and Corasick, 1975) finds every occurrence of any of a set of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patterns in one pass over a text, in O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":" + "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"z"}]},{"type":"text","text":") for "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":" symbols and "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"z"}]},{"type":"text","text":" matches: a trie of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patterns with failure links. Its "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/statesView-swift.property","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is the automaton as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let automaton = AhoCorasickAutomaton(patterns: [\"he\", \"she\", \"his\", \"hers\"])","automaton.matches(in: \"ushers\").map(\\.patternIndex)   \/\/ [1, 0, 3]"],"syntax":"swift"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tries"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tries over sequences of any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" symbols, with prefix queries, and multi-pattern matching."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"references":{"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/Trie":{"url":"\/documentation\/tries\/trie","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"Trie","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Trie","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Trie","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A set of sequences kept in a trie: a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose root-to-vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"paths spell the keys (Fredkin, 1960)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie","type":"topic"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries":{"type":"topic","title":"Tries","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/tries","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tries over sequences of any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" symbols, with prefix queries, and multi-pattern matching."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries","role":"collection"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/Trees":{"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trees","type":"topic","title":"Trees","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/trees","abstract":[]},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/RadixTreeDictionary":{"title":"RadixTreeDictionary","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/radixtreedictionary","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A dictionary keyed by sequences, kept in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): a trie in which every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"chain of vertices with one child and no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"symbols, each key’s vertex holding its value."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RadixTreeDictionary"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RadixTreeDictionary"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/AhoCorasickAutomaton/StatesView-swift.struct/symbol(ofEdgeAt:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"symbol","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"ofEdgeAt","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Symbol","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/StatesView-swift.struct\/symbol(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/ahocorasickautomaton\/statesview-swift.struct\/symbol(ofedgeat:)","role":"symbol","title":"symbol(ofEdgeAt:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The symbol a goto edge reads, or nil for a failure edge."}]},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/RadixTree":{"url":"\/documentation\/tries\/radixtree","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"RadixTree","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RadixTree"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RadixTree"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A set of sequences kept in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): a trie in which every chain of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices with one child and no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its symbols."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree","type":"topic"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/TrieDictionary":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrieDictionary"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary","type":"topic","title":"TrieDictionary","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrieDictionary"}],"url":"\/documentation\/tries\/triedictionary","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A dictionary keyed by sequences, kept in a trie: a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"root-to-vertex paths spell the keys, each key’s vertex holding its value (Fredkin, 1960)."}]},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/AhoCorasickAutomaton/statesView-swift.property":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/ahocorasickautomaton\/statesview-swift.property","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The automaton’s states as a directed graph: a vertex per state, numbered from 0 for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"root, a goto edge from each state to each of its trie children, and a failure edge from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each state but the root to its failure state. "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/StatesView-swift.struct\/symbol(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" tells the two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"apart."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"statesView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Tries20AhoCorasickAutomatonV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Symbol","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">.","kind":"text"},{"text":"StatesView","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Tries20AhoCorasickAutomatonV10StatesViewV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"title":"statesView","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/statesView-swift.property","type":"topic","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Symbol","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}]}},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/AhoCorasickAutomaton":{"url":"\/documentation\/tries\/ahocorasickautomaton","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An automaton that finds every occurrence of every pattern of a set in one pass over a text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(Aho and Corasick, 1975)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton","type":"topic"}}}